        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "ee723a51-c84e-56f4-8bf3-56c24938cb7e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Beecher's Handmade Cheese\n- People: Kurt Beecher Dammeier\n- Places: Pike Place Market, Seattle, Washington, New York City's Flatiron District, Elliott Bay waterfront, United States\n- Topics: Public markets, artisan cheesemaking\n\nFacts:\n- Pike Place Market is a public market overlooking the Elliott Bay waterfront in Seattle, Washington, United States.\n- Pike Place Market opened on August 17, 1907, and it is one of the oldest continuously operated public farmers' markets in the United States.\n- Kurt Beecher Dammeier founded Beecher's Handmade Cheese in 2003.\n- After obtaining a difficult-to-obtain storefront lease in Pike Place Market, Kurt Beecher Dammeier opened Beecher's Handmade Cheese there.\n- Beecher's Handmade Cheese is an artisan cheesemaker and retail shop with locations in Pike Place Market in Seattle, Washington, and in New York City's Flatiron District.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
